{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Its taste</b> (4): and its taste was like the taste of rich cream. \"Moab has been at ease from his youth and settled on his lees\" (Jeremiah 48:11) — therefore its taste stood in it; \"its taste changed\" — when its taste changed regarding David: Moab, who was settled, its taste stood; but David, who went into exile from place to place, changed his taste. And the wilderness generation, even though they went from place to place, did not change their taste on account of the manna, concerning which it is stated \"and its taste\" — for the Torah was given only to the eaters of the manna."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:49.788201766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}